# Defect 522, 2026-10-09 (lane b16-compiler; defect 469's other half): a
# chain of structs past 32 deep, each level's value built in one body. clang
# asks of every assignment of a struct whether it holds a `const` field, by a
# walk that costs the square of the structs it holds by value, so the front
# end cost the cube of the depth: 3.39, 18.75 and 130.96 billion instructions
# at 250, 500 and 1,000 levels of this shape. Past the depth `typeorder` hands
# clang a chain from its bottom, the unit now defines `HERO_COPY`, and each
# assignment of one of its own structs is a byte copy whose two sides are
# asserted one type: 1.61, 3.69 and 9.87. This case is 40 levels, every odd
# one held through an option: each level built, stored, loaded, and read
# back down through its case's payload and field, the copies' every site,
# and the values compared whole. Its blessed emission shows the copies.
variant R0
    a
        v: i64
    b

variant R1
    a
        inner: R0?
    b

